Z||000000||CoolBlue87GT||07-26-2001||04:26 PM||||Finally got around to fixing the headlight door for the drivers side motor.<P>Oh boy what fun !  Took about an hour.<P>Got my best tools out !<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00099.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00102.jpg">  <BR>Remove headlight assembly<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00106.jpg">  <BR>Remove side cover<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00107.jpg">  <BR>One thing the instructions dont say, put down a rag to catch all the 'crap'.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00108.jpg">  <BR>After all this,it works !!   The hardest part was removing the cast alum part off the shaft with the gear.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 07-26-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||LT1 Chop Top||07-26-2001||04:33 PM||||I did the same w/ Dickmans replacement bushings......very easy and worked perfectly!||||reg||1
Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||07-26-2001||05:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B>I did the same w/ Dickmans replacement bushings......very easy and worked perfectly!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep, that's were mine came from.<P>I guess I'm lucky it wasn't the passenger side.  That looked harder.  It works fine.  <P>||||reg||1
