Z||000006||theogre||07-26-2001||07:21 PM||||One thing to add to above.... if the drive shaft binds/drags the hole coming out, STOP!<P>The end of the shaft often is flaired by the end. Right where the D shaped area is at the end of the flatened section.<P>If you don't file off that flair then you damage the berring in the motor body.||||reg||1
Z||000007||CoolBlue87GT||07-26-2001||10:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by coolcat:<BR><B>What was wrong with the headlight door.BTW whats up with the plunger your car got a clog?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The bushings needed to be changed, the door was not going up every time.<P>The plunger ?  It had a fur ball !!||||reg||6
